## Look hardest at
- The race test is the reason this item exists. Would it actually FAIL against a
  non-atomic implementation? A test that asserts "no error" or that tolerates
  two winners proves nothing. Check it asserts exactly one `claimed`, seven
  denied, and a final stored assignee equal to the winner — and that it runs
  under `-count=5`.
- Is every cell of the ladder covered: open→claimed, held-unexpired→denied with
  `deny_reason=held` and NO write, self→renewed, expired→stolen with the prior
  holder in the event, `in_progress` with empty stored assignee→claimed,
  a non-claimable status (e.g. `blocked`)→denied with `deny_reason=status`,
  empty/whitespace `assignee` argument→error, closed→error, no-lease claim never
  expires?
- The "denial writes nothing" test: does it really check `updated_at`, the
  events table AND `dirty_issues`, or only one of the three?
- Is the pre-027 migration case built in code rather than as a committed fixture
  database?
- Tests that assert on implementation details instead of behavior, or that would
  pass with the feature deleted.

